---
interface Props {
  kind:
    | "siblings"
    | "orchestrator"
    | "ownership"
    | "handoff"
    | "recovery"
    | "workshop"
    | "boundary"
    | "shadow"
    | "wrongness"
    | "scattered";
}

const { kind } = Astro.props;
const titleId = `concept-figure-${kind}`;
const svgTitleId = `${titleId}-svg-title`;
const svgDescId = `${titleId}-svg-desc`;
---

{
  kind === "orchestrator" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">02 / Gas City SDK</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>Gas City SDK: one operating system for agent work</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1100 620"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>Gas City SDK component map</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          Rigs, agent templates, and named sessions feed a flow from formulas
          through the Beads work record, dispatch, session pools, and receipts.
          Repair and reaper controls inspect the entire flow.
        </desc>

        <g class="svg-primitives">
          <rect class="svg-box" x="60" y="50" width="250" height="88" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="82" y="82">Isolate projects</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="82" y="112">Rigs</text>
          <rect class="svg-box" x="425" y="50" width="250" height="88" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="447" y="82">Define worker roles</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="447" y="112">Agent templates</text>
          <rect class="svg-box" x="790" y="50" width="250" height="88" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="812" y="82">Address workers</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="812" y="112">Named sessions</text>
          <path class="svg-link" d="M310 94 H425 M675 94 H790" />
        </g>

        <g class="svg-pipeline">
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Describe">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="20" y="225" width="190" height="110" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="42" y="258">Describe</text>
            <text class="svg-label" x="42" y="295">Formula</text>
          </g>
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Remember facts">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="235" y="225" width="190" height="110" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="257" y="258">Remember facts</text>
            <text class="svg-label" x="257" y="293">Work record</text>
            <text class="svg-small" x="257" y="317">Beads</text>
          </g>
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Route">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="450" y="225" width="190" height="110" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="472" y="258">Route</text>
            <text class="svg-label svg-label--wrapped" x="472" y="288">
              <tspan x="472" dy="0">Dispatcher +</tspan>
              <tspan x="472" dy="23">hooks</tspan>
            </text>
          </g>
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Run">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="665" y="225" width="190" height="110" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="687" y="258">Run</text>
            <text class="svg-label" x="687" y="293">Session pools</text>
            <text class="svg-small" x="687" y="317">named sessions</text>
          </g>
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Verify + record">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="880" y="225" width="190" height="110" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="902" y="258">Verify + record</text>
            <text class="svg-label svg-label--wrapped" x="902" y="288">
              <tspan x="902" dy="0">Review +</tspan>
              <tspan x="902" dy="23">receipts</tspan>
            </text>
          </g>
          <path class="svg-link" d="M210 280 H235 M425 280 H450 M640 280 H665 M855 280 H880" />
        </g>

        <g class="svg-repair">
          <path class="svg-link svg-link--dashed" d="M115 385 V420 H985 V385" />
          <g class="svg-labelled-box" data-label="Repair + reapers">
            <rect class="svg-box" x="300" y="455" width="500" height="100" rx="10" />
            <text class="svg-label" x="328" y="495">Repair + reapers</text>
            <text class="svg-small" x="328" y="526">stale claims · sessions · branches · handoffs</text>
          </g>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <ul class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Gas City SDK components">
        <li>Rigs isolate repositories and their agent worker pools.</li>
        <li>Agent templates define generic worker roles.</li>
        <li>Named sessions give running workers stable addresses.</li>
        <li>Formulas describe steps and dependencies in the Beads work record.</li>
        <li>Dispatchers and hooks claim eligible work and wake session pools.</li>
        <li>Agent sessions execute work, then reviews and gates record outcomes.</li>
        <li>Repair and reaper controls inspect stale claims, sessions, branches, and handoffs.</li>
      </ul>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Gas City connects durable work facts, execution, evidence, and repair.
        Packs and installations can add their own coordinating roles around it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "workshop" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">06 / Live result loop</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>How finished work reaches an exact acknowledgement</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1120 640"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>OutcomeReady workshop flow</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          Agents, formulas, and orders write canonical work facts to the
          Beads work record. A verified result enters an OutcomeReady outbox, a
          durable completed-result record awaiting acknowledgement. A Temporal
          Outcome Workflow delivers and redelivers it until the mayor verifies
          evidence, records an exact acknowledgement, and Beads stores the
          acknowledged receipt.
        </desc>

        <g class="svg-flow">
          <rect class="svg-box" x="31" y="65" width="232" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label" x="49" y="120">Agents, formulas,</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="49" y="147">and orders</text>

          <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="313" y="65" width="219" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label" x="331" y="123">Beads work record</text>
          <text class="svg-small" x="331" y="153">canonical work record</text>

          <rect class="svg-box" x="582" y="65" width="221" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label" x="600" y="123">Verified result</text>
          <text class="svg-small" x="600" y="153">tests + evidence agree</text>

          <rect class="svg-box" x="853" y="65" width="236" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--wrapped" x="871" y="112">
            <tspan x="871" dy="0">OutcomeReady</tspan>
            <tspan x="871" dy="23">outbox</tspan>
          </text>
          <text class="svg-small" x="871" y="164">pending acknowledgement</text>

          <path class="svg-link" d="M263 130 H313 M532 130 H582 M803 130 H853" />

          <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="853" y="300" width="236" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label" x="871" y="355">Temporal Outcome</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="871" y="382">Workflow</text>

          <rect class="svg-box" x="582" y="300" width="221" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--wrapped" x="600" y="340">
            <tspan x="600" dy="0">Mayor verifies</tspan>
            <tspan x="600" dy="23">evidence</tspan>
          </text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-small--wrapped" x="600" y="392">
            <tspan x="600" dy="0">human handoff</tspan>
            <tspan x="600" dy="19">remains visible</tspan>
          </text>

          <rect class="svg-box" x="313" y="300" width="219" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--wrapped" x="331" y="340">
            <tspan x="331" dy="0">Exact</tspan>
            <tspan x="331" dy="23">acknowledgement</tspan>
          </text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-small--wrapped" x="331" y="392">
            <tspan x="331" dy="0">generation +</tspan>
            <tspan x="331" dy="19">session fence</tspan>
          </text>

          <rect class="svg-box" x="31" y="300" width="232" height="130" rx="10" />
          <text class="svg-label" x="49" y="355">Beads acknowledged</text>
          <text class="svg-label" x="49" y="382">receipt</text>

          <path class="svg-link" d="M971 195 V300 M853 365 H803 M582 365 H532 M313 365 H263" />
          <path class="svg-link svg-link--dashed svg-link--flow" d="M971 430 V515 H692 V430" />
          <text class="svg-small" x="671" y="548">wait durably · redeliver while pending</text>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <ol class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="OutcomeReady workshop flow">
        <li>Agents, formulas, and orders update work.</li>
        <li>Beads stores the canonical work record.</li>
        <li>A verified result is ready for delivery.</li>
        <li>The OutcomeReady outbox stores a durable completed-result record awaiting acknowledgement.</li>
        <li>The Temporal Outcome Workflow delivers, waits durably, and redelivers while pending.</li>
        <li>The current mayor verifies evidence.</li>
        <li>An exact acknowledgement binds the result generation and agent session.</li>
        <li>The Beads acknowledged receipt becomes canonical.</li>
      </ol>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Beads records what happened to the work. Temporal records the procedure
        that keeps a finished result pending until someone acknowledges it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "ownership" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">03 / New boundary</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>Who owns what</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1000 440"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>Ownership after the Temporal integration</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          The Beads work record owns mutable task facts, the Temporal Workflow owns
          durable procedure, and Temporal Activities contain nondeterministic
          work and external calls.
        </desc>
        <rect class="svg-box" x="45" y="70" width="270" height="245" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="70" y="110">Application record</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="70" y="145">Work record: Beads</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="188">task facts · claims</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="218">dependencies · artifacts</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="248">outcomes · receipts</text>

        <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="365" y="70" width="270" height="245" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="390" y="110">Durable procedure</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="390" y="145">Temporal Workflow</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="390" y="188">Event History · waits</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="390" y="218">retries · cancellation</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="390" y="248">signals · progress</text>

        <rect class="svg-box" x="685" y="70" width="270" height="245" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="710" y="110">Nondeterministic work</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="710" y="145">Temporal Activities</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="710" y="188">agent processes · tests</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="710" y="218">reviews · external calls</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="710" y="248">heartbeats · fences</text>
        <path class="svg-link" d="M315 192 H365 M635 192 H685" />
      </svg>

      <ul class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Ownership boundaries">
        <li>The Beads work record owns mutable task facts, claims, dependencies, artifacts, outcomes, and receipts.</li>
        <li>The Temporal Workflow owns Event History, deterministic decisions, waits, retries, cancellation, signals, and progress.</li>
        <li>Temporal Activities contain agent processes, tests, reviews, external calls, heartbeats, and fences.</li>
      </ul>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Beads remains the source for task facts. Temporal gives the
        procedure a durable owner and routes side effects through Activities.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "recovery" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">05 / Recovery invariant</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>One agent session survives Worker loss</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1000 440"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>One agent session across a Worker restart</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          One Worker schedules an Activity and binds an agent. After that Worker
          dies, another Worker replays the Workflow state and resolves the same
          agent session by its stable identity and claim token, then reattaches
          to that generation-fenced session. The heartbeat carries progress, not
          the identity, so this holds even when the Worker died before the first
          heartbeat landed.
        </desc>
        <path class="svg-link" d="M100 210 H900" />
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="100" cy="210" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="100" y="217">1</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="100" y="285">Schedule Activity</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="100" y="313">stable identity</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="300" cy="210" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="300" y="217">2</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="300" y="285">Bind one agent</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="300" y="313">heartbeat progress</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step svg-step--failure" cx="500" cy="210" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="500" y="217">×</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="500" y="285">Worker dies</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="500" y="313">agent keeps running</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="700" cy="210" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="700" y="217">3</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="700" y="285">Replay + resolve</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="700" y="313">by stable identity</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="900" cy="210" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="900" y="217">4</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="900" y="285">Reattach</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="900" y="313">one fenced receipt</text>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <ol class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Agent recovery sequence">
        <li>A Worker schedules the Activity with stable identity.</li>
        <li>The Activity binds one agent and heartbeats progress.</li>
        <li>The Worker dies while the agent session keeps running.</li>
        <li>A replacement Worker replays the Workflow state and resolves the existing session by its stable identity and claim token, which holds even if no heartbeat was ever recorded.</li>
        <li>The retry reattaches, picks up progress from any recorded heartbeat, and accepts one generation-fenced receipt.</li>
      </ol>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Workflow replay recovers orchestration state. Start-or-attach and a
        generation fence prevent a duplicate agent or stale completion.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "siblings" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">01 / Two instantiations</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>One SDK, two ways to survive a crash</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1000 470"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>Gas Town and the Temporal-backed city as siblings</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          The same Gas City primitives support two separate arrangements. Gas
          Town recovers by letting a fresh agent infer another valid path from
          the durable work record. The Temporal-backed city recovers by replaying
          a recorded procedure. Neither was added to the other.
        </desc>

        <rect class="svg-box" x="215" y="330" width="570" height="106" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="245" y="368">Shared foundation</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="245" y="400">Gas City primitives</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="245" y="424">work record · agents · sessions · formulas · dispatch</text>

        <path class="svg-link" d="M400 330 V295 H255 V250" />
        <path class="svg-link" d="M600 330 V295 H745 V250" />

        <rect class="svg-box" x="60" y="120" width="390" height="130" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="88" y="158">Gas Town</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="88" y="192">Nondeterministic Idempotence</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="88" y="220">a fresh agent infers another valid path</text>

        <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="550" y="120" width="390" height="130" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="578" y="158">This city</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="578" y="192">Durable replay</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="578" y="220">the recorded procedure is replayed</text>

        <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="500" y="70">siblings, not layers</text>
        <path class="svg-link" d="M450 185 H550" />
      </svg>

      <ul class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Two instantiations">
        <li>Gas City supplies the shared primitives: the work record, agents, sessions, formulas, and dispatch.</li>
        <li>Gas Town is one arrangement of them, recovering through Nondeterministic Idempotence, where a fresh agent infers another valid path.</li>
        <li>The Temporal-backed city is a sibling arrangement, recovering by replaying a recorded procedure.</li>
        <li>Neither was added to the other.</li>
      </ul>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Both arrangements are built from the same primitives. They differ only in
        what they promise will survive a crash.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "handoff" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">04 / Durable handoff</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>A crash between claim and launch is survivable</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1000 440"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>Transactional outbox into Signal-With-Start</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          One Beads transaction writes both the ready transition and its delivery
          event. A bridge reads the pending event and calls Signal-With-Start
          under a stable Workflow ID. If the bridge dies before acknowledging the
          outbox, the event is delivered again and the Workflow ignores an event
          ID it has already processed.
        </desc>

        <path class="svg-link" d="M120 150 H880" />
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="120" cy="150" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="120" y="157">1</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="120" y="225">One transaction</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="120" y="253">state + event together</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="373" cy="150" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="373" y="157">2</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="373" y="225">Bridge reads event</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="373" y="253">from the outbox</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="627" cy="150" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="627" y="157">3</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="627" y="225">Signal-With-Start</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="627" y="253">stable Workflow ID</text>
        </g>
        <g>
          <circle class="svg-step" cx="880" cy="150" r="36" />
          <text class="svg-step-number" x="880" y="157">4</text>
          <text class="svg-label svg-label--center" x="880" y="225">Signal or start</text>
          <text class="svg-small svg-label--center" x="880" y="253">one operation</text>
        </g>

        <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="230" y="312" width="540" height="112" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="258" y="348">If the bridge dies here</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="258" y="380">the event arrives again and the</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="258" y="406">Workflow ignores an ID it has seen</text>
      </svg>

      <ol class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Durable handoff sequence">
        <li>One Beads transaction writes the ready transition and its delivery event together.</li>
        <li>A bridge reads the pending event out of the outbox.</li>
        <li>The bridge calls Signal-With-Start under a stable Workflow ID derived from the city, run, and work item.</li>
        <li>Temporal signals the existing Workflow or starts it with the signal, in one operation.</li>
        <li>If the bridge dies before acknowledging the outbox, the event is delivered again and the Workflow ignores an event ID it has already processed.</li>
      </ol>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The crash window is not closed, it is made boring. Stable identity turns
        redelivery into expected behavior instead of a duplicate launch.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === "boundary" && (
    <figure class="concept-figure" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
      <header class="concept-figure__header">
        <p class="concept-figure__index">07 / Remaining work</p>
        <h3 id={titleId}>What Temporal owns, and what it leaves behind</h3>
      </header>

      <svg
        class="concept-figure__svg"
        viewBox="0 0 1000 460"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby={`${svgTitleId} ${svgDescId}`}
      >
        <title id={svgTitleId}>The boundary of Temporal's guarantee</title>
        <desc id={svgDescId}>
          Temporal owns the durable procedure, waits and timers, retry
          scheduling, cancellation, and acknowledgement state. The application
          still owns exactly-once external effects, whether the code is correct,
          repair of a corrupt work record, worktrees and disk, and approval
          policy for external actions.
        </desc>

        <rect class="svg-box svg-box--accent" x="40" y="60" width="440" height="360" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="70" y="102">Inside the guarantee</text>
        <text class="svg-label" x="70" y="136">Temporal owns</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="188">durable procedure and its history</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="228">waits and timers</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="268">retry scheduling</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="308">cancellation</text>
        <text class="svg-small" x="70" y="348">acknowledgement state</text>

        <rect class="svg-box" x="520" y="60" width="440" height="360" rx="10" />
        <text class="svg-eyebrow" x="550" y="102">Still application work</text>
